<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gestapo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1933">1933</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Geheime Staatspolizei</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gestapo was the secret state police of Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, created in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hermann-goring">Hermann Göring</a> in 1933 and taken over by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-himmler">Heinrich Himmler</a>, under whose SS it extended across the Reich and occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Operating outside judicial control, it hunted political opponents, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and resisters, using informers, torture and detention in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camps</a>. It took a central part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a> and was declared a criminal organisation at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> trials.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gestapo.jpg" alt="Gestapo" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-R97512,_Berlin,_Geheimes_Staatspolizeiamt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Terror was organised by the SS under Heinrich Himmler, which absorbed the police, ran the <b>Gestapo</b> and the concentration camps from Dachau, opened in March 1933, onwards, and in 1939 combined its security services in the Reich Security Main Office under Reinhard Heydrich.</blockquote><a href="/empire/nazi-germany">Nazi Germany · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1933 the <b>Gestapo</b> shut it; Mies won permission to reopen, but he and the faculty then agreed to close the school themselves.</blockquote><a href="/movement/bauhaus">Bauhaus · Course of Events</a></li><li><blockquote>Companys was handed over by the <b>Gestapo</b> and executed in 1940.</blockquote><a href="/state/generalitat-of-catalonia-1931-1939">Generalitat of Catalonia (1931-1939)</a></li></ul></section>
